msgid "| 2026-08-06 | Residual-suite pass (sweep close-out) | The update wave's remaining active-fixture adapters, suite-verified: seo-mappers 11 (**AIOSEO 4.9.10→5.0.0.1 MAJOR confirmed compatible** — the suite drives the panel against AIOSEO's own model; Yoast 28.2 + SEOPress 10.1 also covered), media-folders 20 (FileBird 6.5.7), tec-panel 8 (TEC 6.17.2), cache-purge 11 (Breeze 2.5.12), activity-log-status 20 (Simple History 5.30), meta-box-panel 19 (Meta Box 5.14). All green, zero fixes needed. Sweep cycle fully closed: backlog empty, fixture debt clear. Unranked future candidates on record: Really Simple SSL 9.7 posture provider (plugin-support waves), GoSMTP stays a documented skip (free build stores no logs). |"
msgstr ""

#: docs/adapter-coverage.md:201
msgctxt "docs/adapter-coverage.md"
msgid "| 2026-08-06 | Ship top 1: FluentSMTP 2.3.0 catch-up (all three slices) | Resend now rides their __MA_DOC_TOKEN_1__ — __MA_DOC_TOKEN_2__ + the __MA_DOC_TOKEN_3__ trail record, headers/attachments restored, cc/bcc dropped on redirects, no duplicate log row (__MA_DOC_TOKEN_4__); gated on the __MA_DOC_TOKEN_5__ column so a pre-2.3.0 build keeps the __MA_DOC_TOKEN_6__ fallback and can never half-send through a failing update. New parameterized \"Resend to…\" action (comma-separated override, all-or-nothing validation; detail-modal only — list rows render field-less actions by design). Detail sections gain a Resends trail (via their __MA_DOC_TOKEN_7__; their unserialize refuses objects). ConnectionHealth (2.3.0) feeds a status-card row (All passing / N failing / Not checked yet) and a System health row (__MA_DOC_TOKEN_8__: all-failing = fail, some = warn, spliced after AIOS). Caps resolve through __MA_DOC_TOKEN_9__ (their helper when present). Suites: mail-log 30→36, fsmtp-settings 8 green. E2E: real Mailpit deliveries, override + 400 path, their checkAll() against the live connection. |"
msgstr ""

#: docs/adapter-coverage.md:205
msgctxt "docs/adapter-coverage.md"
msgid "| 2026-08-06 | WC 11.0 deep pass (ship top 1, second slice) | All 10 ecommerce suites run sequentially against WooCommerce 11.0.0: 153/153 green, zero console errors, WC Subscriptions 9.0.1 compatible. Changelog audit of the 11.0.0 section: removals are the product block editor feature/routes (Gutenberg-side; Minimal never used them) and several WC admin notices relocated into Site Health (their nag reduction; nothing to wire). No wc/v3 or Analytics API surface changes. **No code change** — the ops backlog item closes as verified. |"
msgstr ""

#: docs/adapter-coverage.md:203
msgctxt "docs/adapter-coverage.md"
msgid "| 2026-08-06 | WPForms Pro entries adapter (ship top 1, fourth slice — the last big forms name) | adapters/wpforms.php: full forms-family treatment. Reads = prefix-scoped SELECTs (search LIKE over the fields JSON); WRITES through their __MA_DOC_TOKEN_1__ handler (update/delete — hooks fire, delete cleans entry_fields + entry_meta, verified rows-left=0). Caps defer to __MA_DOC_TOKEN_2__ (view_entries/edit_entries/delete_entries; editor = 403 + hidden surface, empirically checked). HARD-WON: __MA_DOC_TOKEN_3__ column is UTC (14:22 stored at 10:22 EDT) → emit ISO Z + column utc:true; display status derives spam/trash-win-else-viewed; opening a detail marks viewed through their update (their screen's behavior; never for spam/trash); their __MA_DOC_TOKEN_4__ search machinery deliberately NOT used (advanced-search complexity; LIKE matches their fallback). Star/unstar as when-gated actions on a '★' item key. Registers only when the entry handler exists (Lite = nothing). SUITE GOTCHA: execSync + __MA_DOC_TOKEN_5__ with a JSON.stringify'd arg lets the shell expand __MA_DOC_TOKEN_6__/__MA_DOC_TOKEN_7__ to empty — the suite's wp() helper writes a temp file + __MA_DOC_TOKEN_8__; and the forms-family detail modal is a CONTACT CARD (renderEntryDetail — no \"Answers\" heading; assert card content). Suites: wpforms 16, forms-status 14. |"
msgstr ""

#: docs/adapter-coverage.md:200
msgctxt "docs/adapter-coverage.md"
msgid "| 2026-08-06 | scrutoscope: onto their 1.5 list API (vendor-reported, GitHub issue #3) | Axis B, prompted by the plugin author. Scrutoscope 1.5.0 added __MA_DOC_TOKEN_1__ specifically so integrators stop reading the table; list now rides it through __MA_DOC_TOKEN_2__ (gated on __MA_DOC_TOKEN_3__, the shaper their contract names), status totals via __MA_DOC_TOKEN_4__. **The win is not tidiness: their output Sanitizer runs on that path and did not run on ours** (reduced SQL + host-only HTTP URLs are re-applied at read time as defense-in-depth for rows written by older builds; a direct SELECT is what skips it). Same pass fixed a self-inflicted gap: Minimal's own \"Profile this hook\" writes __MA_DOC_TOKEN_5__ but the tabs were pinned/session/background, so Minimal's captures were findable under All profiles only. Added the On demand tab plus a Context column from __MA_DOC_TOKEN_6__. Column read kept for pre-1.5. Suite scrutoscope 29→34. |"
msgstr ""

